// G2 adjudication ledger — APPEND ONLY. One JSON object per line.
//
// Each line records that a named HUMAN asked one question about one exact piece of text:
//
//   "Describe an implementation that passes EVERY clause of this acceptance criterion and does NOT
//    deliver the stated business purpose. Barred: 'they might compute it wrongly' — the
//    implementation must be one a competent, lazy team would actually ship."
//
// It does NOT record that they answered it well. scripts/check_g2_adjudication.py checks the
// paperwork and nothing else; it must never be cited as a check on requirement quality.
//
// Fields (all required):
//   req_id            the register row, e.g. "REQ-PPM-004"
//   hash              sha256 of the row's normalised (Business purpose \x1f Acceptance) cells.
//                     Edit either cell and the adjudication LAPSES — that is the point.
//   adjudicator       a human handle from 02_requirements/g2_adjudicators.json. "MODEL:..." is
//                     rejected: this is the one gate a model cannot answer for itself.
//   disposition       AMENDED (an exploit existed — the acceptance was rewritten so it fails) or
//                     REBUTTED (name the clause that blocks the obvious exploit, in a full sentence)
//   reasoning         >= 120 characters. The exploit, or the clause that blocks it. A cost, not a
//                     proof: a fluent wrong rebuttal passes as easily as a correct one.
//   amendment_commit  required for AMENDED — the commit that carries the rewritten acceptance
//   adjudicated_at    ISO date
//
// Duplicate (req_id, hash) keys are REJECTED, not last-line-wins: appending must never erase a
// prior finding.
//
// EMPTY BY DESIGN at creation (2026-08-13), because recording an adjudication retrospectively
// would be recording a human act that did not happen, in a ledger whose only purpose is to prove
// it did.
//
// It did not stay empty until the Wave-18 planning gate, as this header first predicted. The
// structure block (REQ-PPM-006 .. -010) was adjudicated within hours of THIS LEDGER being created
// on 2026-08-13, ahead of the gate, so the gate has cleared rows to choose from. (Said of the ROWS
// rather than the ledger it would be false for one of them: REQ-PPM-006 was written on 2026-08-12,
// in re-baseline part 1.) Eight entries cover five rows: 006 was adjudicated three times and 007
// twice, after their text was rewritten. That is the lapse rule working as designed, not a
// duplicate -- and 006's two re-adjudications are different acts, one substantive (the swap and
// commitment pair proved unbuildable) and one presentational (the plain-language rewrite).
{"req_id": "REQ-PPM-006", "hash": "8330ef217826e82290798f9b5b881ed5cbbe708983b1feedbfe7a7b5995704ed", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit: register a ONE-MEMBER measure vocabulary. Every clause passed -- the key carried a measure type, every family declared NOTIONAL and refused a synthetic other, the census found no undeclared consumer -- while no holding anywhere carried two exposures. Amended so the second measure IS the acceptance: two measures with a distinct producer each, differing on a holding where they are economically distinct (swap notional vs market value, OR commitment funded vs unfunded -- either), with coincidence explicitly not a failure where the measures legitimately coincide.", "amendment_commit": "2ef2896", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-13"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PPM-007", "hash": "323aa25aeccdee42692f2eff921f5ee1be393c6934a7b2691a7f31c123eb8b46", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit: declare every contract, mark one family NOT AGGREGATABLE, implement the refusal in a helper -- exact set equality holds and the refusal fires in test, while production aggregates in a read view that consults nothing. No family refuses anything; a helper does, and nothing calls it (the LQ-1 inert-control finding). Amended to require EVERY aggregation site to be bound to a contract lookup, asserted by census, and the refusal to fire through the public read surface. Deliberately not 'only one aggregation site', which would reject a correct build that aggregates in both SQL and Python. The duration example was also corrected: duration aggregates by market-value weighting and belongs in WEIGHTED, not NOT AGGREGATABLE.", "amendment_commit": "30d7e9a", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-13"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PPM-006", "hash": "5f1c7d69d82ed3bca1e24d772edac36b714959a451e2747a69d2cbd0a26987b5", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Re-adjudicated after the row was rewritten. The original exploit was a one-member measure vocabulary. The first amendment named a swap and a commitment as the demonstrating pair; reading the model showed InstrumentTerms cannot express a swap and unfunded sits outside the exposure grain, so neither was buildable. The row now requires a bond's notional exposure against its market-value exposure, both from data already captured, differing on any bond not priced at par, and requires exposure_type to join the uniqueness key, which it is missing today. Swap and commitment pairs are recorded as trigger-bound follow-ons.", "amendment_commit": "161a64a", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-13"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PPM-008", "hash": "ea5076840904f104e6f4093bdb69ab25fbc18d682c6c3d4811f56bc3fa47a4c8", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit: implement node-scoping on a two-level tree, the only shape that exists today. Parent-equals-children is trivially true with one level of nesting, so no middle layer is ever tested. Amended to require a test tree at least three levels deep with more than one node type, checking the top total against both the level below and the level below that. The user's question about two-level portfolios then found a defect in the wording, so the row now states that trees of any depth are valid and that minimum depth is a property of the test, never a rule applied to data.", "amendment_commit": "f0d6ad4", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-13"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PPM-009", "hash": "6ef2cd55173c866898a429459db9c5df627187905b4ce6ed90a12abf7e468e39", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "The user rejected the row's premise: mandate compliance is a compliance function, not risk management. SCOPE-03 declares the risk coverage as market, credit, counterparty, liquidity, scenario/stress and limits/breach, and guideline monitoring is not among them, so the row was doing work the scope document does not claim. A mandate rule engine would also duplicate the shipped limit framework with only a different owner. Narrowed to the half that is genuinely risk work: the portfolio name must not be treated as data, because aggregation that groups by a stale label produces wrong concentration and factor numbers. The mandate half is declined with two recorded triggers, superseding the Q4 answer ratified the previous day.", "amendment_commit": "5363f1a", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-13"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PPM-010", "hash": "83546c8f8754c6ec836202e427f7124145a8fb0884d226e30ebc8b94c1c770e0", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit: ship against a single-currency book, where every clause is vacuously true because there are no translated legs at all. Amended to require a three-currency test book, an assertion that the translated-leg count exceeds zero before anything is claimed about the legs, and a total compared against a hand-computed value. Reading the code then changed two clauses: the same-currency path is already an exact no-op in shipped code, so that clause is relabelled a regression guard rather than work; and triangulation is recorded but never labelled, being only inferable from there being two legs. The user chose the option that also requires a reader to see the conversion path on a screen, since fx_legs reaches the API and no screen renders it.", "amendment_commit": "b90df22", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-13"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PPM-006", "hash": "406e373f4e3259c78406ae16bcc5b527e146020ead62e939d499cfba1bb91350", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Re-adjudicated after a plain-language rewrite that changed presentation only. The substance is unchanged: two exposure measures with a producer each, demonstrated by a bond's notional against its market value from the valuation path, differing on any bond not at par, with coincidence explicitly not a failure and exposure_type required in the uniqueness key. The amendment history moved into notes at the end so the requirement a builder must satisfy comes first. Re-approved because the register's failure mode was criteria nobody attacked, and a criterion that has to be parsed twice will not be attacked properly.", "amendment_commit": "1c75510", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-13"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PPM-007", "hash": "17825b14a71b8f86fe3ce85ab163f0819ef8019522cd1b4e1b367f0a0668f553", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Re-adjudicated after a plain-language rewrite that changed presentation only. The substance is unchanged: exact set equality of contracts against the registry, every aggregation site bound to a contract lookup with more than one site permitted, the NOT AGGREGATABLE refusal firing through the public read surface, mixed measure types refused, and the duration correction now on its own line rather than inside a parenthesis where it was easier to miss. Re-approved on the same reasoning as PPM-006.", "amendment_commit": "1c75510", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-13"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PPM-001", "hash": "daff82703337026678073097b18ef72e1ccdc2bc0257517d1e8504f4338ff29a", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit: a table with a parent id nothing traverses passes every clause -- persistence is an INSERT, tenancy is the RLS every table gets, the anchor is prose, and the requirement cell said VERSIONED nodes while no clause tested versioning. Amended to require three levels and two node types exercised by REQ-PPM-008's rollup test over this entity, and history-stable reads: re-parenting a node between a run and a read must not change the run's stored view of the tree. The entitlement half stays deferred and is stated as deferred, never counted as delivered.", "amendment_commit": "5050d8a", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-15"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PPM-002", "hash": "c2664cb42b8a5d5d6eb05a00dddccfd11e9721d11b30b86ad3228bca484cf77a", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit: as-of reconstruction shipped and green while nothing tests SINGLE source -- the next analytic can ingest its own holdings CSV and the row stays green. Amended to require a census of holdings-consuming code paths in which every governed family resolves holdings through the position master's as-of reconstruction at the pinned snapshot, checked by exact set equality rather than subset (the RPT-3 defect). Reconstruction survives as a regression guard only.", "amendment_commit": "5050d8a", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-15"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PUB-002", "hash": "a31d89ca46f364f49510825cba37cea8e78c00f1df07dd2f034cf286dbe1b306", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit: the shipped state plus one table -- captured curves read back byte-identical (stored data reproduces trivially) and interpolation_method is captured as an inert label with no engine (OQ-P2-5-9), so the row was held open by Status prose, not its criterion. Amended to require an off-node query computed by the declared method against a hand-computed oracle, different declared methods giving different off-node values, a non-zero interpolated-read count asserted first, and at least one governed consumer that discounts with it.", "amendment_commit": "5050d8a", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-15"}
{"req_id": "REQ-MKT-002", "hash": "577ede00cca52a21d63dd8f87ce6784d89d3efcbec8553969026b745b6780c9b", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit: reproduce-within-epsilon names no oracle, so any deterministic code passes at epsilon zero -- including the book-level curve-node DV01 already shipped at P3-1 -- and nothing required position grain, so nothing supported a hedge. REQ-PPM-004's defect shape verbatim, on the feeder row for risk decomposition. Amended to require position-grain sensitivities composing to the book figure under the declared operator, a hand-computed external oracle per convention, and a bump-one-position test moving the book by the stated sensitivity within a DECLARED tolerance.", "amendment_commit": "5050d8a", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-15"}
{"req_id": "REQ-LIM-002", "hash": "361f93cc28b342c7766db3b120b784c43dc9c7eb970fae3d1496ddf747de191a", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit: the shipped breach comparison already reproduces and binds, but a comparison is not a measure -- nothing stored or served the ratio, so nobody could see 87 percent and act before the breach, and ENT-032 could stay reserved forever. Amended to require utilization as a stored governed number (observed, threshold, ratio) readable through the rule-7 entity/time surface with visible trend, and a demonstrating value strictly between zero and the threshold, because a fixture at only zero or breach never exercises usage.", "amendment_commit": "5050d8a", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-15"}
{"req_id": "REQ-SCN-003", "hash": "98c32dd963d0ad6d0cf345b92d7a47e5ab3acaa54cbff2422c73a0b8098b17ae", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit: REQ-PPM-004 verbatim -- run the shipped linear factor shock alone, label the run COMBINED, bind whatever it consumed; reproduces and binds while private sleeves, carrying no factor exposures, pass through unshocked under unnamed-factor-unchanged semantics with clean coverage counts. Amended to require a private holding whose leg is asserted non-zero, ablation showing each of the three legs changes the total, and a declared combination method with its interaction limitation stated.", "amendment_commit": "5050d8a", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-15"}
{"req_id": "REQ-CRD-005", "hash": "53c25a3728efd4f2a0922d218554c0d6f9d2162610178fab8ea14775e4873cfe", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit: reproduce-from-a-pinned-snapshot was already passable by the curve-node spread-DV01 shipped at P3-1 against a fixture curve -- everything the row was minted to prevent when split from CRD-003. Amended to require position-grain CS01 composing to the book figure, a hand-computed oracle on a known bond over a known spread curve, and a demonstrating curve that is a captured EXTERNAL curve asserted by ORIGIN provenance. The row stays trigger-parked; amended now because the ledger lapses automatically if the text moves again.", "amendment_commit": "5050d8a", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-15"}
{"req_id": "REQ-LIQ-004", "hash": "542eb7a2007a89bf7b1ca35113a9042deb5e577ad157a6ca54b2907f34a66a77", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit: a constant forecast reproduces perfectly, and feeds-CFP-indicators named an artifact defined nowhere in the register, so it could never fail -- both clauses passed with no forecasting delivered. The Status also read bare Draft while CC-2 had shipped the per-pair kernel (ENT-059) on 2026-07-20, the OQ-LQ-1-12 register-silence class. Amended to require the portfolio-level rollup CC-2 itself named as v2, a driver-sensitivity test where differing commitment terms produce differing projections, and the undefined clause deleted.", "amendment_commit": "5050d8a", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-15"}
{"req_id": "REQ-RPT-001", "hash": "cf2f55108accaf2ea4c1cf2b22d19ab7a3cc8744c0c326e63d6b8bf1a0b4c27d", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit: the acceptance named no family set, so it was fully satisfied by the four built families while only a sentence of Status prose held the row open for credit -- binding scope held in an editable comment, which is how REQ-PPM-004 drifted. Narrowed to exact set equality between the families the reproduction proof exercises and REPORT_FAMILIES (a subset check is the RPT-3 defect), with the credit report minted as REQ-CRD-008 and homed with the Q6 credit build so each row closes honestly.", "amendment_commit": "5050d8a", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-15"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PPM-001", "hash": "be4bb760d8adea070b9380543c5e4701f4a35a1a84f0c24d177b9abc49532182", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit against the pre-amendment text: STRUCT-3's full-subtree snapshot pin satisfies the entire versioning clause on its own -- the re-parent-between-run-and-read test passes because the tree was serialized into the run's snapshot, while the hierarchy entity keeps NO history and the tree as-of yesterday is unanswerable outside a run. The requirement cell said VERSIONED edits; no test clause exercised version history independent of a run. Amended so the entity's OWN history is the acceptance: the tree resolves as-of a past time by timestamp alone, no run or snapshot in scope. Re-adjudication directed by the owner 2026-08-15 at the STRUCT-1 close (the prior entry lapsed when its own amendment commit 5050d8a moved the hash).", "amendment_commit": "725e2fe", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-15"}
{"req_id": "REQ-INT-001", "hash": "eda69d983e6152235ee5080907041ef2fee78698eb06fc1c45225b436823225e", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit against the pre-amendment text: the acceptance covered upload validation only -- 'bad/malicious files rejected; lineage origin + audit recorded' -- and explicitly deferred canonical mapping, so a team ships a validating uploader that writes generic staged JSON forever and the row is fully satisfied while no client data ever becomes a position. The row's own purpose word is 'onboard data', and nothing tested onboarding. A second exploit survived the first draft of the repair and is closed by clause (7): every listed outcome was satisfiable by a hand-authored mapping JSON, which deletes the AI-proposes/human-ratifies leg that is the ratified INGEST-1 thesis and its whole model-governance cost. Amended to ten outcome clauses: refusal without a ratified mapping, hard-FK binding on batch AND row, an edited-mapping differential, mechanical write-path discovery, per-operation refusals fired with unsupported operations refused by name, four-eyes ratification, proposing-model attribution, three distinct operation kinds, reproducibility naming all three inputs (mapping, file, and the code-lookup reference data), and a restatement refusal.", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-20", "amendment_commit": "32e88a5"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PRS-001", "hash": "a55a595f1ec3322dc09ad4415e7dc3bb72a7af389c994230f3bb2d773063ad7f", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit against the pre-amendment text: a stub contract for every family -- mark 'table', identity ['run_id'] -- satisfies exact set equality, the added-family clause and the identity-field clause while NOTHING reads any contract. That is the declaration-without-firing shape ratified decision D2 forbids, proposed one wave after D2 was ratified. Amended so the contract must be CONSUMED: the section's pinned content carries the contract the render used, a regenerated historical report renders the PINNED contract, and a declared-precision change moves the bytes of a NEW report while leaving every prior report byte-identical on regeneration -- both halves asserted. The pinning half is not decoration: a render-time lookup would make one precision edit mark every pre-edit report DIVERGED in the CTRL-018 reproduction sweep, because every render input is pinned by shipped invariant. Also adds a declared exclusion vocabulary, since a presentation contract for REPRODUCTION is meaningless and the census would otherwise force a dishonest stub.", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-20", "amendment_commit": "32e88a5"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PRS-002", "hash": "86b90dd09bc66fb9e64fb152bf8f0a8b701572244553a3dbe414838203ed0acd", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit against the pre-amendment text: all four clauses -- byte-identical re-render, carries the run id, altering an input moves the bytes, covered by the report content hash -- are satisfied by a renderer that never consults a presentation contract and emits an SVG containing only <text> number dumps. That is a table drawn in SVG. The word 'chart' appears in the title and is nowhere defined by marks, and no clause connects this row's renderer to PRS-001's contracts. Amended to require the SVG be produced FROM the family's pinned contract (asserted by generating either side of a contract edit) and to contain the declared MARK SHAPES for its declared mark type -- path, rect, line or circle -- not only text nodes.", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-20", "amendment_commit": "32e88a5"}
{"req_id": "REQ-RPT-001", "hash": "8088e3d06236ca21cb2ec133613d809efe94039523dca9b3e8d3e28d9a8ded20", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "The 2026-08-15 narrowing bound scope to exact set equality against REPORT_FAMILIES, and that binding is itself an editable code constant, so the exploit it closed re-opened in a new form: when a family turns out to be awkward to add, do not add it -- equality still holds over the four that exist -- and deleting a family passes too. That is the same editable-scope drift the narrowing was written to close, one level down. Separately 'the families the reproduction proof exercises' had no defined referent: the register's own Status cell names the deployed script, which seeds exactly ONE of four families, so the unit-tier reading is nearly free while the deployed reading is four to five times the per-family scaffolding. Amended to name the deployed proof artifact explicitly and to make declining to add a family a FAILURE of this row rather than a way to keep the equality true.", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-20", "amendment_commit": "32e88a5"}
{"req_id": "REQ-ADM-001", "hash": "cfb132b48378ae705f6dc5653de345984a127e0a0c5215c32a9a5c8dc8a2a743", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Exploit against the pre-amendment text: 'Principal comes from OIDC; MFA enforced (AD-007)' is prose with no delivered form, and the row has sat In-Progress since Wave 9 with the OIDC leg real and the deployed posture untouched. The obvious repair carries its own exploit, which is why the delivered clause is worded as it is: 'the deployed stack refuses dev_header over HTTPS' is passed by ANY 401, because with auth_mode=oidc the dev-header branch is never reached and every unauthenticated call 401s -- so the clause names the SPECIFIC dev-header refusal. The amendment also RETAINS the MFA commitment, which an earlier draft of this very gate silently dropped: AD-007 is Accepted with the CISO as approver, THR-01's stated mitigation is that MFA, and the lever (oidc_require_mfa + oidc_acr_values) is shipped and merely ships off. Retiring a CISO-approved clause by omission at a planning gate is precisely the quiet-lapse class the re-baseline diagnosed. Scope bounded: internet-facing hosting and enterprise IdP federation stay RTM-P9, and the existing dev_header proof stack must keep passing its four deployed proofs, because those scripts create their principals over HTTP at runtime and can carry no IdP identity.", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-20", "amendment_commit": "32e88a5"}
{"req_id": "REQ-PPM-002", "hash": "307bf7993e32c0d7b02b9b8eef48805501cdd6ebd792a30a343261e4b819b16a", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "Re-adjudicated because the 2026-08-15 amendment's own hash lapsed and because this wave HOSTS the census. Residual exploit in the amended text: 'a census of holdings-consuming code paths checked by EXACT SET EQUALITY' is satisfied by comparing a hand-written list against a hand-written list, which is circular -- the set equality proves the two lists match, not that either matches the code. STRUCT-2's census 2 exists precisely because of this and discovers aggregation constructs mechanically, never a hand list. Amended with one clause: the consuming set is DISCOVERED MECHANICALLY. The timing matters -- the amendment's own rationale is 'the next analytic ingests its own holdings CSV', and the ingestion slice is this wave.", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-20", "amendment_commit": "32e88a5"}
{"req_id": "REQ-RPT-004", "hash": "7e6e84da14b3a83c46d50588e25f1c9016b9cf7967bd3bc77a1b54470c758ba1", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "REBUTTED", "reasoning": "No amendment needed; the acceptance already blocks the obvious lazy build. The exploit a competent lazy team would ship is a definition entity that is written but never bound -- generations carry a definition id that no renderer consults, or an edit mutates the row in place so 'versioned' is a column rather than a fact. Both are blocked by named clauses: 'editing a definition mints a NEW version rather than mutating the old, asserted by RE-READING THE PRIOR VERSION AFTER AN EDIT AND FINDING IT UNCHANGED' is a differential a mutating implementation provably fails, and 'a generation bound to version N re-renders from N's declarations AFTER N+1 EXISTS' is a second differential that fails for any renderer reading current state. The clause that carries the row is the second one: it is unsatisfiable without real version isolation. Entering scope at Wave-19 S2 in place of a fifth report family, per the re-baseline's own instruction that this entity is built before the other reporting rows.", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-20"}
{"req_id": "REQ-ADM-001", "hash": "8526f0d5507cd38c780201ff4ac64e658239f283728ef7da04dcac7879bbb635", "adjudicator": "ghostai8088", "disposition": "AMENDED", "reasoning": "RE-ADJUDICATED at the ratification review fold, because the amendment adjudicated earlier the same day (hash cfb132b4..., amendment_commit 32e88a5) contained a STRUCTURALLY UNFIREABLE refusal -- the CON-1 class, written into a clause whose whole purpose was to close an exploit. That clause demanded the deployed target refuse a dev-header request 'BY THE DEV-HEADER REFUSAL SPECIFICALLY', to block the bare-401 exploit. But under auth_mode=oidc control never reaches the shim branch (deps.py:99), and both dev-header-specific refusals in the tree are guarded on auth_mode=='dev_header' (deps.py:102-105, config.py:63-68), so a dev-header request to an OIDC target raises the opaque 'invalid credentials' 401 at deps.py:179-180 -- precisely the bare 401 the clause rejects. No implementation of the planned slice could have satisfied it, and the slice's own build list did not create any new refusal. The repair names the refusal that DOES fire (the boot-time AD-007 RuntimeError when auth_mode='dev_header' meets app_env != 'local') and makes the runtime half an explicit build obligation: either build a dev-header rejection distinguishable from a missing-credential 401, or assert the header is provably never consulted. Second defect closed in the same pass: the MFA clause was refusal-only, and a refusal-only clause is satisfied by a target that admits nobody -- it now carries both arms (P18), a token lacking the required acr REFUSED and a token carrying it ADMITTED.", "amendment_commit": "7d4cc93", "adjudicated_at": "2026-08-20"}
